{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8329": {
      "title": "Performing Arts Program - Assistant Director of Theatre for Musical Productions",
      "description": "Performing Arts Program - Assistant Director of Theatre for Musical Productions | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Performing Arts Program - Assistant Director of Theatre for Musical Productions Req #933 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 7, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Sunday, November 8, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Assistant Director of Theatre for Musical Productions provides artistic, musical, and operational leadership for the musical components of the Theatre Arts Program within the Division of Student Affairs. This non-academic position works closely with the Director of Performing Arts to develop high-quality theatrical programming, support student participation and development, fulfill Theatre Arts Program grant requirements, and expand recruitment and outreach efforts. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Musical and Artistic Leadership Provide oversight and leadership for all musical elements of the Theatre Arts Program. Serve as musical director, conductor, and/or piano accompanist for up to three full theatrical productions each semester, as well as ancillary events presented by the Theatre Arts Program. Prepare, organize, and distribute all musical materials required for seasonal productions, rehearsals, auditions, and performances. Coordinate music rehearsal schedules for all productions and events involving music. Assist with the artistic leadership and implementation of Theatre Arts Program productions and programming. Maintain and grow a comprehensive library of music, scores, recordings, and related materials that is organized and accessible to students. Student Support and Program Administration Be available daily to assist, advise, and support students participating in the Theatre Arts Program. Oversee and encourage student involvement in productions, performances, rehearsals, and other program activities. Serve as a liaison for Theatre Arts Program students and support students in understanding and fulfilling their TAP grant obligations. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and supportive environment that promotes student engagement, artistic growth, accountability, and a strong sense of community. Assist the Director of Theatre with the creation and implementation of new programs and student activities, including student-led productions and performances. Recruitment and Retention Participate fully in the recruitment of prospective Theatre Arts Program students. Interview and audition incoming and prospective students seeking Theatre Arts Program grants and participation in the program. Represent the Theatre Arts Program at recruitment events, auditions, open houses, and other University programs. Develop and maintain relationships with high school theatre programs, educators, students, and community partners to increase awareness of the University’s Theatre Arts Program. Support outreach and recruitment initiatives designed to attract talented and engaged students to the program. Work with the Director of Theatre to focus on retention of Theatre Arts students through individual meetings and workshops Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree in music, musical theatre, theatre arts, performing arts, or a related field required; master’s degree preferred. Demonstrated experience in musical direction, conducting, and piano accompaniment. Experience working with theatrical productions, rehearsals, auditions, and performances. Strong organizational skills and the ability to coordinate multiple productions, rehearsal schedules, and deadlines. Ability to work effectively with college students and provide appropriate guidance, mentorship, and support. Strong interpersonal, communication, collaboration, and leadership skills. Experience with student recruitment, audition processes, or high school theatre outreach preferred. Availability to work evenings and weekends as required by rehearsals, performances, auditions, and special events. Unusual Working Conditions Varied schedule, including nights and weekends. This position reports to the Director of Theatre Arts and collaborates closely with Theatre Arts Program staff, production personnel, students, University departments, and external partners. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $50,000-$70,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8322": {
      "title": "Notre Dame Prep",
      "description": "Notre Dame Prep - Head Coach Strength & Conditioning | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Notre Dame Prep - Head Coach Strength & Conditioning Req #934 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, October 4, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, resume, or curriculum vitae, along with the contact information for three letters of reference, who will be contacted only if you are selected for an interview. Only applications submitted via our Career portal will be considered. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Strength & Conditioning Coach is responsible for developing and implementing strength and conditioning programs for student-athletes across various sports. This role focuses on enhancing athletic performance, reducing the risk of injury, and promoting overall fitness among high school student-athletes. This is a part-time, seasonal position running approximately mid-August through mid-June each academic year. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Develop sport-specific strength and conditioning programs for the athletic teams Implement and supervise strength and conditioning programs for the athletic teams, both in-season and off-season Educate athletes on the importance of strength training, conditioning, nutrition, and recovery strategies Assist with scheduling the use of the weight room Teach proper lifting techniques and exercise forms to ensure student-athlete safety and effectiveness Provide individualized coaching to student-athletes, focusing on skill development and injury prevention Monitor progress and adjust training programs as necessary Recommend equipment enhancements to the athletic facilities as it pertains to performance Maintain a safe training environment, ensuring all equipment is properly maintained and all safety protocols are followed Stay informed about and comply with relevant regulations and guidelines concerning student-athlete health and safety Work collaboratively with coaches, athletic trainers, and other staff to ensure a comprehensive approach to student-athlete training and recovery Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) or equivalent certification through an accredited sport science organization (NASM, NCCA) is required. Previous experience coaching strength and conditioning at the high school or collegiate level is required. Strong knowledge of exercise physiology, sports nutrition, and injury prevention Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Ability to motivate and inspire student-athletes Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Proficient in using strength and conditioning equipment and technology Current CPR/AED and First Aid certifications required Unusual Working Conditions The work schedule will include evenings and weekends based on team schedules and events. Physical demands may include lifting weights, demonstrating exercises, and standing for extended periods. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a fingerprint-supported background check and a DCF/CPS background screening. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $8,000 - $9,000. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Employment Indicator Part-time Seasonal Scan this QR code and apply! Download 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8311": {
      "title": "Notre Dame Prep",
      "description": "Notre Dame Prep - Head Coach Boy's Lacrosse | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Notre Dame Prep - Head Coach Boy's Lacrosse Req #935 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, October 4, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, resume, or curriculum vitae, along with the contact information for three letters of reference, who will be contacted only if you are selected for an interview. Only applications submitted via our Career portal will be considered. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Head Coach is responsible for leading, developing, and managing a competitive sports team at Notre Dame Prep. This position requires strong leadership skills, a deep understanding of the sport, and the ability to cultivate an environment that promotes sportsmanship, teamwork, and personal growth among student-athletes. The Head Coach will oversee all aspects of the team’s operations, including practice schedules, game preparation, athlete recruitment, and coordination with other school departments to ensure the team's success and well-being. The Head Coach will serve as a role model for student-athletes, promoting the school’s mission and values both on and off the field. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Team Leadership and Coaching: Plan, organize, and conduct daily practices to develop the skills, fitness, and teamwork of athletes. Lead and motivate student-athletes, ensuring they are focused, disciplined, and respectful both on and off the field. Set clear goals and expectations for the team, and work with student-athletes to achieve them. Ensure that all team members understand the strategies, tactics, and skills necessary to compete at a high level in the sport. Promote teamwork, sportsmanship, and a positive attitude among athletes. Game Preparation and Management: Develop game strategies and ensure that the team is prepared for competition. Supervise and manage all aspects of game day, including team warm-ups, player substitutions, and in-game coaching adjustments. Work with the Athletic Director to schedule games, tournaments, and other competitions. Coordinate with opposing teams, officials, and event organizers to ensure smooth execution of games and events. Player Development and Recruitment: Develop individualized player development plans to help athletes improve their skills and reach their full potential. Monitor the academic performance of athletes, ensuring they meet academic eligibility requirements and maintain a balance between athletics and academics. Foster a positive and supportive environment that encourages student-athletes to excel academically, athletically, and personally. Team Administration and Communication: Maintain up-to-date records on athletes’ progress, team performance, and other relevant data. Communicate regularly with athletes, parents, and school administration about practice schedules, game schedules, and team-related matters. Hold regular meetings with team members to discuss performance, goals, and any issues that may arise. Assist in organizing team events such as team-building activities, banquets, and fundraisers. Compliance and Safety: Ensure the team adheres to all school, league, and state regulations and policies, including eligibility requirements, safety guidelines, and sportsmanship expectations. Monitor the physical health and safety of student-athletes, ensuring that proper precautions are taken during practice and games. Work closely with athletic trainers and medical staff to ensure that athletes receive proper treatment and rehabilitation when necessary. Ensure all equipment is properly maintained and meets safety standards. Return all equipment at the conclusion of the season. Collaboration with Athletic Department: Work closely with the Athletic Director and other coaches to develop the overall athletic program and promote a positive, inclusive sports culture within the school. Attend departmental meetings and contribute to the overall goals of the athletics program. Support and encourage the involvement of other coaches and athletes in school events and activities, fostering a sense of community across the athletic department. Work collaboratively with faculty and staff to ensure that student-athletes maintain a healthy balance between their academic and athletic responsibilities. Community and Alumni Engagement: Promote the team and the athletic program to the broader school community, including alumni, parents, and supporters. Represent the team and the school at Open House, community events, alumni gatherings, and other relevant functions. Foster a culture of pride and support for the team, encouraging school spirit and fan engagement. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes A Bachelor's degree in Physical Education, Sports Management, or a related field is preferred. At least 3-5 years of coaching experience at the high school or collegiate level, with a proven record of success in the sport. Head coaching experience is preferred. First Aid/CPR certification is required. Skills: In-depth knowledge of the sport, including its rules, strategies, and techniques. Strong leadership, motivational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to develop and implement effective training programs and game strategies. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively with athletes, parents, and school staff. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage time effectively. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, supportive, and competitive team culture. Knowledge of safety protocols and injury prevention in sports. Other Qualifications: A strong commitment to the mission and values of Notre Dame Prep, with a focus on character development, sportsmanship, and academic excellence. Ability to work with students of diverse backgrounds and skill levels. Ability to maintain composure and professionalism under pressure, particularly during competitions. Strong understanding of the importance of balancing academics and athletics for student-athletes. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information regarding student-athletes. Unusual Working Conditions Evening and weekend work is required for practices, games, and tournaments. Travel may be required for away games or competitions. Frequent outdoor activity and time spent in various weather conditions, depending on the sport. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a fingerprint-supported background check and a DCF/CPS background screening. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this seasonal position is $6,500-$7,500. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Athletics Pay Type Salary Employment Indicator Part-time Seasonal Travel Required Yes Scan this QR code and apply! Download 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8240": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Accounting, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Adjunct Instructor - Accounting, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) Req #60 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, October 4, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Accounting & Information Systems in the AACSB-accredited Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructors committed to preparing students to use financial knowledge and sound judgment to guide the future of business and society. At Sacred Heart, adjunct instructors bring accounting expertise into an applied learning environment that connects financial theory with professional practice. The role offers a meaningful opportunity to shape the next generation of accounting professionals by helping students develop technical knowledge, analytical judgment, and the ability to deliver accurate financial insight across business, government, education, and law. Undergraduate and graduate offerings include a Bachelor of Science in Accounting , an accelerated bachelor’s-to-master’s pathway, a Master of Science in Accounting , and specialized minors and certificates in accounting fundamentals, business analysis and reporting, forensic accounting, and tax compliance and planning. Students can also prepare for the AICPA Examination and gain applied experience through opportunities such as Volunteer Income Tax Assistance . Additional information about available classes can be found in the Accounting & Information Systems course descriptions . Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate or graduate accounting courses in accordance with established course objectives and academic standards Create an engaging and supportive learning environment Connect accounting concepts and principles with current professional practice Provide students with timely feedback and maintain regular communication throughout the course Collaborate with the department chair and faculty as appropriate Fulfill all responsibilities associated with the assigned course Qualifications: A minimum of a master’s degree in accounting or a closely related field Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred Strong verbal, written, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive environment in which all members of the University community can thrive and succeed Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8100": {
      "title": "Club Sports Ice Hockey Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Club Sports Ice Hockey Assistant Coach | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Club Sports Ice Hockey Assistant Coach Req #897 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Sacred Heart University Department of Club Sports and Recreation is seeking an Assistant Coach for the Men’s Ice Hockey team. The Assistant Coach will be responsible for supporting the head coach with duties related to the team. This is a part-time position that will run from September 1st to May 15th of each academic year Principal Duties & Responsibilities Assist in the development and execution of practice plans, game strategies, and overall team management. Focus on the skill development of athletes, offering individual and group instruction tailored to improve performance. Aid in identifying and recruiting talented players, attending games, and evaluating potential recruits. Help manage the team during games, contribute to strategic decisions, and ensure effective communication among players and coaches. Assist with logistical aspects such as scheduling, travel arrangements, equipment management, and compliance with league and school regulations. Provide guidance and support to athletes on and off the field, fostering a positive and motivating environment. Ensure adherence to safety protocols, support injury prevention and management efforts, and promote overall athlete well-being. Facilitate clear and effective communication between players, coaches, and support staff. Represent the team in community events, fostering good public relations and building support of the program. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Minimum of 3 years coaching experience at the high school, prep, junior or collegiate level Bachelor’s degree preferred Must be willing to work nights and weekends, as the vast majority of games are Friday-Sunday Possess experience working with diverse staff, including college-age students Must maintain coaching certification or be willing to acquire certification CPR/First Aid Certification Unusual Working Conditions Nights and weekends will be required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $4,000 - $4,500. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Athletics Pay Type Salary Employment Indicator Part-time Seasonal Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Travel Required Yes Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
