    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7823": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Management, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Adjunct Instructor - Management, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) Req #61 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Management in the AACSB-accredited Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructors committed to developing mindful, innovative leaders prepared to strengthen organizations and make a positive impact on business and society. Adjunct instructors join an interdisciplinary community of accomplished scholars and seasoned practitioners with expertise spanning strategy, organizational behavior, entrepreneurship, innovation, human resource management, operations, supply chain management, business law, and international management. Drawing on academic and professional experience, instructors create active and engaging learning experiences where students apply established frameworks to real organizational challenges and strengthen the judgment, leadership, teamwork, and ethical decision-making skills needed in a changing global landscape. Management offers undergraduate and graduate programs, including a Bachelor of Science in Management, an MBA, and specialized minors and graduate certificates. Additional information about available classes can be found in the Management course descriptions . Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate or graduate management courses in accordance with established course objectives and academic standards Create an active, engaging, and supportive learning environment Connect management concepts and established frameworks with relevant organizational and business challenges Provide students with timely feedback and maintain regular communication throughout the course Collaborate with the department chair and faculty as appropriate Fulfill all responsibilities associated with the assigned course Qualifications: A minimum of a master’s degree in management, business, or a closely related field Academic or professional expertise relevant to the assigned course Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred Strong verbal, written, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive environment in which all members of the University community can thrive and succeed Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use 