revention and management efforts, and promote overall athlete well-being. Facilitate clear and effective communication between players, coaches, and support staff. Represent the team in community events, fostering good public relations and building support for the program. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Minimum of 3 years coaching experience at the high school, prep, junior or collegiate level Bachelor’s degree preferred Must be willing to work nights and weekends, as the vast majority of games are Friday-Sunday Possess experience working with diverse staff, including college-age students Must maintain coaching certification or be willing to acquire certification CPR/First Aid Certification Unusual Working Conditions Nights and weekends are required Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $5,400 - $6,000 Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a communit